# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=
# Two providers, hybrid by necessity:
#   Gemini (free key at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey) handles everything except
#   real web search: regulatory retrieval scoring, regulatory explanation, and
#   vendor/financing JSON extraction. Its own Google Search grounding tool needs a
#   billing-enabled Google Cloud project even on an otherwise-free API key, so it isn't
#   used here.
#   Groq (free key at https://console.groq.com/keys) runs the actual vendor/financing
#   web search via groq/compound, which stays reachable on a plain free key.
#
#   GEMINI_REASONING_MODEL - gemini-flash-latest. Use the "-latest" alias, not a pinned
#     version (gemini-2.5-flash, gemini-2.5-flash-lite): pinned older model ids can 404
#     with "no longer available to new users" depending on when your API key/project
#     was created. Thinking cannot be disabled on this tier (thinking_config with
#     thinking_budget=0 returns 400 INVALID_ARGUMENT) -- hidden reasoning tokens count
#     against max_output_tokens, so every call budgets generously or output truncates.
#     Free tier is also capped low (5 requests/minute per model at time of writing) --
#     expect RESOURCE_EXHAUSTED bursts under repeated testing.
#   GROQ_SEARCH_MODEL - groq/compound, runs a real search server-side and returns
#     evidence in message.executed_tools (list of {type, arguments, output,
#     search_results:{results:[{title,url,content,score}]}}).
GEMINI_REASONING_MODEL=gemini-flash-latest
GROQ_SEARCH_MODEL=groq/compound
